# Keep secrets, the private journal, and local-only files OUT of the Docker
# build context. Without this, the build-stage `COPY . .` bakes them into
# intermediate image layers and the BuildKit cache on a local operator build.
# (The final images are clean — multi-stage copies only the compiled binary —
# but the build-stage layer is recoverable via `docker history` / cache export,
# so the tokens and journal would leak if that layer is ever pushed or shared.)
#
# Only clearly-sensitive or build-irrelevant paths are listed. Go sources,
# go.mod/go.sum, and the embedded internal/db/migrations/*.sql stay in context.

# Secrets & runtime config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The private journal database — the whole asset; never put it in build context
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Version control & CI (not needed to compile)
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Local-only agent brain (already gitignored; keep out of the image too)
.agents
.claude
AI_CONTEXT.md
CLAUDE.md

# Build / coverage artifacts
coverage.out
